From: ReForge <reforge@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] overlayfs: declare MODULE_IMPORT_NS for the VFS internal namespace

The Tina BSP backports v5.6's per-symbol namespace exports for VFS helpers
(__kstrtabns_dentry_open, __kstrtabns_vfs_link, etc are present in the
running stock kernel's /proc/kallsyms — symbols belong to the namespace
VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver). It does NOT
backport the corresponding fs/overlayfs/ MODULE_IMPORT_NS declaration
(upstream commit f3e57aac4262 added it in v5.7-rc1).

Without this declaration the kernel emits build-time warnings:
  WARNING: module overlay uses symbol vfs_rename from namespace
           VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver,
           but does not import it.
...and at LOAD time refuses the .ko with -EINVAL ("Unknown symbol vfs_link").

Add the import to fs/overlayfs/super.c right next to the existing
MODULE_LICENSE/MODULE_AUTHOR/MODULE_ALIAS_FS declarations.

This is the minimal fix to make overlay.ko loadable on the stock 5.4.61
BSP kernel running on the AD5M.
---
--- a/fs/overlayfs/super.c
+++ b/fs/overlayfs/super.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Miklos Szeredi <miklos@szeredi.hu>");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Overlay filesystem");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
+MODULE_IMPORT_NS(VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver);
 
 
 struct ovl_dir_cache;
